Create a function called divide_safe with a, b:
    If b is equal to 0:
        Raise error "Division by zero is not allowed"
    Return a / b

Try:
    Print "Attempting 10 / 2..."
    Set result to divide_safe(10, 2)
    Print "Result:", result

    Print "Attempting 10 / 0..."
    Set bad_result to divide_safe(10, 0)
    Print "This will not be printed"
Catch error as err:
    Print "Safely caught error:", err
Finally:
    Print "Cleanup in finally block executed successfully."

Print "\nProgram continues executing normally after caught error!"
